1\. Right now, you're inside your body, experiencing life through your eyes.

2\. Scientists create a clone of you.

3\. You want yourself — the exact person experiencing this moment right now — to somehow go into that clone.

4\. When it happens, you open your eyes in the clone and experience life from there, just as you're experiencing life right now.

5\. The clone doesn't merely become a copy of you. You become the one living in that body.

6\. You're not talking about copying your memories, personality, thoughts, or behaviour. You're talking about transferring your actual self, your eternal soul, and your first-person experience into the clone.

7\. The question is: What would make your exact self transfer into that clone so that you continue experiencing life as you, rather than the clone simply existing as another person?
